 "result_text": "I fixed the bad timestamp in `ms_to_timestamp` in `pysubs2/substation.py`. A time like `1:17:39.995` now comes out as `1:17:40.00`, not `1:17:39.100`.\n\nThe cause was the centisecond rounding. The code split the time into hours, minutes, seconds and milliseconds first, then rounded the milliseconds up to the nearest centisecond. A value like 995 ms rounded to 100 centiseconds, which printed as `.100` without carrying into the seconds. The fix rounds the whole time to the nearest 10 ms first and splits it afterwards, so the carry happens correctly.\n\nI checked two values directly: 1995 ms now gives `0:00:02.00`, and 4660955 ms gives `1:17:40.96`. I didn't run the CLI command from the issue, use the example file, or run the test suite.",
